=================================================
===           SCORE CHANGE LOG                ===
=================================================

Future release:
---------------
* Do not delete bad fixes, but mark them as such. Do not use them for distance
  analysis, but use them for altitude gain.


SCORE XX.XX XX
-----------
* Reduce number of fixes to a maximum number. The default maximum number = 20000
  Fixes near declared turnpoint (< 3 km) will not be deleted. 
  Because of this the resulting number of fixes may be different from the
  set maximum.
* New output message 155: "Number of fixes reduced"
* The -dflt command line parameter will show details on the deleted fixes
* New command line parameter fixm: Limits the number of fixes
  in any soaring block to the given number, with a minimum of 15000

SCORE 24.02 12/06/2024
-----------
* Check IGC file for invalid characters / bad line coding
* new error code 129: Invalid character or line length in IGC file
* new error code 134: Found declaration line in invalid place
* New parameter -digc: provide debug output for IGC file input


SCORE 24.01 23/04/2024
-----------
* Corrected task declaration after start of flight issue



SCORE 20.02 29/07/2020
-----------
* New file stretches.txt: defines stretches for the runs evalulation
* New command line parameters:
  -nruns  : disables runs (stretch) evaluation
  -druns  : Provide debug info for runs algorithm



SCORE 20.02 29/07/2020
-----------
* Triangle calculation: check if flight is closed within a given distance 
* New command line parameter: -tricdX.x: specifies the closing distance (km).
  -tricd0 will disable closed loop checking
  Parameter not included: enable close loop, using dist = 1 km.
* New message #200: "Triangle: no closed segment found"


SCORE 20.01 26/02/2020
-----------
* Bug correction: Path was not included in some plot file names
* Extebded debug info for plotting


SCORE 19.03 24/10/2019
-----------
* Bug correction: Path was not included in some plot file names


SCORE 19.02 20/09/2019
-----------
* Bug correction: included conditin for very short flights


SCORE 19.01 17/09/2019
-----------
* Added triangle calculation
* New command line parameter -ntri: do not calculate triangle
* New command line parameter -tribf[stepsize]: Also use brute force, to verify optimised algo
    SetepSize: optional, sets step size in number of fixes.
* New command line parameter -tribfssXXX: Also use brute force, to verify optimised algo
    XXX: sets step size in seconds.
* New command line parameter -tribfmnsXXX: Also use brute force, to verify optimised algo
    XXX: set the maximum number of steps, to avoid axcessive run time. Step size will be increased
	if required, to obtain given number of steps.
* New command line parameter -dtri:  debug triangle
* New fields in the dat file:
  - Line 43 - 45: triangle legs
  - Line 46     : Triangle total dsiatnce
  - Line 47     : Triangle brute force total dist (debugging)
* New command line parameters latmax, latmin, lonmax, lonmin
    Allow to fix an area for the plot output.
	Use degress.decimal degrees
	All parameters must be specified.
* Day file class rewritten in order to accomodate other types of plots
* new command line parameter:
  -plot:rgn:name
  Will produce combined plots with the given name for the given region
  Name: if containing blanks:can use quotes or underscores:
  -plot:rgn:"Peeters Jan"  -> Must be tested on Linux !!
  -plot:rgn:Peeters_Jan
  Regions:
    BNL
	FRA
	EUR
	MOR:    Morocco
	SAF:    S Africa
	USA
	AUS:    Australia & N Zealand
  Multiple instances of -plot commands are allowed
* New command line parameter -dplot: provides debug info for the plots
* Comment out command line parameters via # after the '-' character.
  Example: -#plot:xx:xx -> the command is commented out
* Compatibility with new IGC file specifications:
  - HDTE
  - HDTM

  
SCORE 18.05 17/08/2018
-----------
* Corrected bug in fix detection from given time: could result in
  array boundary exceedance / segmentation fault.
* Corrected bug: release condition not correctly set in case of
  manual soaring time evaluation.
* Improved validity checking of command line arguments.
* Changed name and format of airfields database
  * New name: airfields_icao.txt
  * Number of fields line removed
  * -onbekend- line removed
  * Header line included
  * Fields separated by tabs instead of :
  * Field sequence altered: icao, name, lat, lon, level, BNL
  * Liga short name field removed
  * Airfield level legend at end removed
  This allows easier editing via Excel. Export file to text, tab separated.


SCORE 18.04 25/07/2018
-----------
