* Included EBSL in de airfields database


SCORE 18.02 07/04/2018
-----------
* Corrected bug in fasttrack calculation: was not restricted to single soaring block


SCORE 18.01 04/12/2017
-----------
* Non IGC certified loggers will now pass the scoring.
  Message "120  Logger type niet bekend: XXX" will be generated, but
  scoring will not be halted.
* adapted color scheme in graphic output.


SCORE 17.05 15/06/2017
-----------
* Corrected bug: declared task start-altitude was not re-initialized ico
  beercan evaluation.


SCORE 17.04 31/05/2017
-----------
Added support for MOP
* Read MOP from IGC file
* New command line parameter -moponly. If set, analyses only flights with
  MOP detection.
* New command line parameter -nomop. If set: does not use MOP value.
* Display MOP on baro graph in light yellow
* "COMB", = max of ENL & MOP at each point
* For engine detection, use filtered COMB. Filter time constant depends
  on type of detection:                    
  ENL only,
  MOP only = ENL only / 3,
  ENL & MOP = ENL only / 2
  From then on, algorithm is the same.
* Added MOP sensor type in txt output, if MOP sensor is installed. 
* Corrected bug in start altitude calculation of Declared Task.
* Check of number of turnpoints for declared task < 200 km included.
* New command line parameter -ndtime: will skip check of task declaration time


SCORE 17.03 07/04/2017
-----------
* Corrected bug in start altitude calculation of Free Flight.


SCORE 17.02 25/02/2017
-----------
* Adapted for non-standard formatting of GPS datum header string.
* New error code 128 "GPS datum format not standard"
* Changed minimum Charronde angle for plotting on map to 150°
* Modified colors on baro to be consistent with colors on flight plot.
* Changed abbreviations on baro and plot to Dutch.


SCORE 17.01 02/12/2016
-----------
* Algorithm rewritten:
  - Converted to cpp
  - New structure
  - New FF Algorithm
  - Altimeter checked for erratic altitude fixes
* New fields in the dat file:
  - Version (name) of the scoring algorithm used
    will also be written ico critical error.
  - IGC name (can be blank if file could not be read or some other errors)
  - Release time
  - Charronde angle.  Can be negative, can be > 360.
  - Optionally: up to 10 strings containing debugging info at the end
  See "README" for a full description of the dat file.
* Moved field IGC file name to the second line.
  If the file could not be read or in case of some other errors this field will
  contain the input file name.
* New command line parameters
  -nograph  : suppresses generation of graphs
  -ddmld<xx>: Free flight minimum leg distance (0->50)
  -dtmld<xx>: Declared task minimum leg distance (0->50)
  -nft      : Do not perform FastTrack scoring ( replacing obsolete -s)
  -nbru     : Do not perform Charronde scoring
  -dflt     : debug flight detection algorithm
  -dalt     : debug altitude & altitude gain algorithm
  -dbru     : debug Charronde algorithm
  -pause    : request a key press to close the console after execution
  -ec<:FN>  : replaces -ie. Write list of error codes to file "FN", then stops.
              If no file name given: writes to stdout.
 * Command line parameter -s replaced by -nft
 * Command line parameter -nknicksm replaced by -nknicks.  The actual number of
   knicks will be about 3x higheer as the given value

  
SCORE 16.01 14/09/2016
-----------
* Detection of turnpoint sectors that have no fix inside the sector, but where
  a line between two fixes runs through the sector.
* Optimisation of start and finish points for maximum distance.
  Height loss calculated as difference between the minimum altitude between start
  soaring block and start point and maximum height between finish and end of
  soaring block.
* Text file adapted to the new scoring method.
* Added switch -dtimeXX : include a delay of XX seconds, in order to test server behavior
  in case of long execution times.
* Added switch -dttotXX : set the execution time to a minimum of the given time XX (seconds).
  If the execution time is shortre, a waiting time is added to obtain the minimum time.
* Added switch -etmaxXXX : set the value of the maximum ENL threshold


